# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Never commit .env.local.
# Both values are safe to expose in the browser — the publishable key only
# grants what Row Level Security allows. The service role key is NOT used
# anywhere in this app; it lives only in the Edge Function's environment.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_xxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# There is deliberately no SMS_API_KEY here, and there never should be.
#
# Vite compiles every VITE_ variable into the JavaScript bundle, so anything
# in this file is readable by anyone who opens the site and presses F12. That
# is fine for the two keys above and fatal for an SMS key, which spends the
# barangay's message allowance.
#
# The SMS keys live as Edge Function secrets instead:
#   supabase secrets set SMS_API_KEY=<your Semaphore API key> SMS_DISPATCH_SECRET=<random hex>
#
# Semaphore is the only SMS provider. SMS_API_KEY is its key and is read by
# the Edge Function from its own environment at run time, never at build time,
# so it is never needed here. See supabase/README.md.

# Resident-side ID re-upload. Default OFF. Only "true" enables it, and it
# also needs the valid_id_replaced_at column from
# supabase/proposals/valid-id-recheck.sql.proposed, so the migration alone
# does not switch the workflow on.
# VITE_ID_REUPLOAD=true
